ne claim, one more outlet.\\n- e258 [third_party_view; The article, citing data compiled by Bloomberg Intelligence; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg Intelligence data put NVIDIA’s server GPU market share at 97% at year-end 2025, up from 95% at year-end 2024.\\n    Quote: the company’s market share has hardly been dented as demand for equipment going into new data centers remains strong. Nvidia had 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to data compiled by Bloomberg Intelligence.\\n- e259 [third_party_view; The article, citing data compiled by Bloomberg; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg-compiled estimates project NVIDIA FY2027 profit of $228 billion, up 90%, and sales of $393 billion, up 82%; the profit estimate rose 13% over the prior three months.\\n    Quote: The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg. The profit estimate, in particular, has risen by 13% over the last three months.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e188; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e260 [third_party_view; The article; original source The article 2026-07-10; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Alphabet and Amazon are increasingly deploying their own custom-made chips, adding competition for NVIDIA in data-center computing.\\n    Quote: For now, that competition — not just from AMD and Intel but also from its biggest customers like Alphabet Inc. and Amazon.com Inc., who are increasingly deploying their own custom-made chips — is a major factor holding back Nvidia’s stock price.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e145, e279; the argument count