hly $16 billion this quarter.\\n    Quote: Its AI chip revenue jumped 143% year over year last quarter to $10.8 billion, and management sees roughly $16 billion this quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e159, e368, e405; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e347 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source Bloomberg survey of Chinese technology companies ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] A Bloomberg survey found Chinese technology companies expect domestic suppliers to receive about 46% of their AI-chip spending over the next year, versus about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: A new Bloomberg survey showed Chinese technology companies expect to allocate roughly 46% of their AI chip spending to domestic suppliers over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e163; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e348 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record revenue of $81.6 billion in fiscal Q1 2027, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e334; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e349 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided fiscal Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, assuming no China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e336, e387, e434; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e352 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] NVIDIA automotive head Xinzhou Wu estimated that autonomous driving accounts for about 0.006% of the 13 trillion miles driven annually worldwide; he gave no estimate period.\\n    Quote: Right now the percentage of autonomous miles among all the mileage driven is probably negligible. I think it’s 0.006%, or something like that.\\n- e353 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] NVIDIA automotive head Xinzhou Wu said computing needs in autonomous driving have been growing roughly 10 times every two years; he did not specify a measurement period.\\n    Quote: As you know, the computer’s growing at such a rapid pace. We talked about Moore’s Law in the semiconductor industry some time ago, but in the autonomous driving segment, the computer need has been growing at a really astonishing pace. Roughly we are talking about 10 times every two years.\\n- e354 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] NVIDIA automotive head Xinzhou Wu forecast that chip prices would likely rise because demand for chips is intense; he gave no amount or timeframe.\\n    Quote: Actually, most likely even the chip price will need to go up, because of this intense demand for every chip everybody can grab onto.\\n- e355 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] NVIDIA automotive head Xinzhou Wu predicted that Level 4 self-driving would become a mainstream experience in less than five years.\\n    Quote: I would say if I need to give a time, I wouldn’t say five years, but less than five years.\\n- e356 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] NVIDIA automotive head Xinzhou Wu said NVIDIA plans to roll out its ADAS technology in all Mercedes vehicles and some other partners’ vehicles across the United States by the end of 2026.\\n    Quote: First of all, by the end of this year, we are rolling out our technology on the ADAS side in all Mercedes vehicles and some other partners as well, all over the United States.\\n- e357 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] NVIDIA automotive head Xinzhou Wu said NVIDIA and Uber are working toward rolling out an L4 service in the next few years; he did not specify a launch date.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, we are also working closely with our partners, for example, Uber. We announced that at GTC, we are trying to roll out our L4 service in the next few years.\\n- e358 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] NVIDIA automotive head Xinzhou Wu said 80% of mass-production automakers were in NVIDIA’s Hyperion ecosystem for Level 4 autonomy; no measurement date was specified.\\n    Quote: Right now, I would say 80% of the mass-production OEMs are in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for L4.\\n- e360 [fact; gurufocus.com; original source Google ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Google has approached neocloud companies about using its TPUs, according to The Information; no date or amount is given.\\n    Quote: Google has approached so-called neocloud companies about using its tensor processing units, or TPUs, according to a report from The Information.\\n- e361 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source Nscale ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Nscale reportedly told Google that its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity; no date or amount is given.\\n    Quote: One provider, Nscale, reportedly told Google that its active proj